# SuperD migrated from superd.anknovate.com to superdeliverygh.com -
# this sends every path on the old domain to the same path on the new
# one (not just the homepage), permanently. Must come before the SPA
# fallback rule below: Netlify _redirects matches top-to-bottom and
# stops at the first hit, and that rule below has no host qualifier so
# it'd otherwise swallow every request, including these, before this
# one ever got a chance to run.
https://superd.anknovate.com/*  https://superdeliverygh.com/:splat  301!

# The site root is the marketing page, not the Flutter app. Both existed
# and had drifted apart: '/' rendered WelcomeScreen (a Dart widget) while
# '/welcome/' served the hand-built page, so the same site showed two
# different front doors. This makes the static page the single one.
#
# Forced (200!) on purpose: an unforced rule loses to a real file, and
# build/web/index.html - the Flutter host page - is exactly that. Only the
# bare '/' is affected; every app route still falls through to the SPA
# rule below and boots the app as before.
/                            /welcome/index.html   200!

/*    /index.html   200
